{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509301-vampire-dark-ages-v20-claw-vs-shield-sword","id":1509301,"title":"Vampire Dark Ages V20: Claw vs Shield + Sword","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-22T10:54:11-07:00","id":1509301,"title":"Vampire Dark Ages V20: Claw vs Shield + Sword","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> I have a question regarding the difficulty to hit with Protean Claws a target that is using a shield and a sword . According to the book, shield adds +1 passive difficulty to a\u200bny attack, and sword also adds +1 passive difficulty in case it is a hand to hand attack. Would it then be a difficulty of 8, or it is not accumulative?<br /> <br /> I assume the answer can also be applied to Serpentis maws. But what about Serpentis tongue (Level 2 Discipline)? Does it count as a hand to hand attack?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.\u200b<br /> <br /> <img title=\"Screenshot 2023-04-22 at 19.30.44.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1190_1682185754583_166\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1190\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1190\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1190&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"Screenshot 2023-04-22 at 19.30.44.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26742-masticore","name":"Masticore","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T06:50:32-07:00","id":1509475,"title":"","content":"I would say yes. Think about it. If your opponent had a swords and shield prepared between, you it would be supremely difficult to claw them, and biting certainly wouldn't be easier. Fortunately the storyteller system is very flexible and so you're free to get rid of these penalties when the context demands it IE you're already wrestling with the guy or you came up behind them or your defences are high enough that you can happily ignore the sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T08:52:45-07:00","id":1509481,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider is that the claws created by Protean are supernaturally strong and sharp, the quote from V20 was:<br /> &quot;These talons are wickedly sharp, able to rend flesh with ease and even carve stone and metal with little trouble.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> So, any opponent attempting to get into melee range with a Protean user won't be able to keep the melee weapon or shield for more than a round or two. Shields break under normal use between mortal combatants, so Protean claws should make quick work of it. Technically since the claws can beat metal, that means you should at the least be able to free hand parry the sword attacks.<br /> <br /> I don't recall the Serpentis powers getting the same sort of description so I wouldn't give them the same bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T10:15:43-07:00","id":1509489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509301-vampire-dark-ages-v20-claw-vs-shield-sword?p=1509481#post1509481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing to consider is that the claws created by Protean are supernaturally strong and sharp, the quote from V20 was:<br /> &quot;These talons are wickedly sharp, able to rend flesh with ease and even carve stone and metal with little trouble.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> So, any opponent attempting to get into melee range with a Protean user won't be able to keep the melee weapon or shield for more than a round or two. Shields break under normal use between mortal combatants, so Protean claws should make quick work of it. Technically since the claws can beat metal, that means you should at the least be able to free hand parry the sword attacks.<br /> <br /> I don't recall the Serpentis powers getting the same sort of description so I wouldn't give them the same bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Try catch a slashing sword with your nails, I dare you. Even if they're two inches long, you'll probably need to be a celerity master to pull such a thing off. <br /> and such shields can break in pieces while still being functional. <br /> <br /> Regarding their ability to cut through metal, yes, it's written like that in the fluff, but I think you really need to consider your damage potential and the durability of items. &quot;metal&quot; is a category that includes soft gold and the most advanced steels mankind has to offer, and to treat them the same is asking for shenanigans. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T14:37:19-07:00","id":1509523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509301-vampire-dark-ages-v20-claw-vs-shield-sword?p=1509489#post1509489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try catch a slashing sword with your nails, I dare you. Even if they're two inches long, you'll probably need to be a celerity master to pull such a thing off.<br /> and such shields can break in pieces while still being functional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Catching someone's sword hand doesn't require being supernatural or having super speed. Once a shield is broken, it doesn't protect the person anymore, which you would know if you ever had a shield break on you in real life.<br /> <br /> I would also point out that some that variants on the Protean claws can allow for bigger and longer versions, leading to things like fangs that are tusks and talons over 6 inches in length.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509301-vampire-dark-ages-v20-claw-vs-shield-sword?p=1509489#post1509489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding their ability to cut through metal, yes, it's written like that in the fluff, but I think you really need to consider your damage potential and the durability of items. &quot;metal&quot; is a category that includes soft gold and the most advanced steels mankind has to offer, and to treat them the same is asking for shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it says the claws can cut through stone, the soft metal argument is somewhat pointless, especially since I can dent gold with my own fingernails. As far as combat shenanigans goes, when a game system or ST has no idea how such things work IRL, that can be far worse. A good example is using the pommel of a sword to pummel an armored opponent. The armor protects from cuts &amp; slashes, but it doesn't always protect against impact damage which is transferred to the wearer of the armor. But it's not like game systems take that into account, they just try to replicate what was cool in a movie or tv show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}